# Dorr Backend Standards

Full guide: `docs/16-STYLEGUIDE.md` | Architecture: `docs/04-ARCHITECTURE.md`

## Layering

Thin controllers → Services → Repositories. Validation in Form Requests. Responses via `ApiResponse`.

## Shared catalog (General/)

Place cross-audience catalog code in `App\...\General\`:
- Controllers extend `CatalogController`
- Services extend `CatalogService`
- Repositories extend `TranslatableRepository`

Entities: Country, Currency, Flag, Language, ServiceCategory, PlatformSetting.

## Module features

Audience-specific code → `Modules/{Admin|User|AI|Provider}/`.

## Routes

- Admin API: `/api/admin/v1/*` + `auth:admin_api`
- User API: `/api/user/v1/*` + `auth:user_api`
- Always use `locale` middleware on API groups

## Do not

- Put business logic in controllers
- Skip Form Request validation
- Create duplicate CRUD outside base classes
- Modify old production migrations — add new ones
- Use Spatie permission middleware until project enables it (currently unused)
